Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: hold the ring lock through WPTR writes

update_wptr() reads ring->cur under preempt_lock but drops the lock before
programming CP_RB_WPTR. In PREEMPT_ABORT, a concurrent a5xx_flush() is
allowed to advance the same ring and program its new WPTR. If the delayed
update_wptr() then writes its earlier snapshot, the hardware pointer moves
backwards, potentially exposing already-consumed ring contents to the CP.

Serialize the snapshot and MMIO update in both writers. This matches the
locking boundary already used by a6xx. Retain a5xx_flush()'s barrier before
the hardware write and leave preemption, priority levels and GPU clocks
enabled and unchanged.

A deterministic host interleaving test demonstrates the stale overwrite
with the old functions and its exclusion with these functions, including
a ring wrap. The SM-T825's observed CP opcode-zero fault with RPTR ahead
of WPTR is consistent with this race, but hardware causality remains to
be established by comparative testing.

Related review discussion (same update_wptr lock boundary):
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2024/08/05/1202

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -33,54 +33,55 @@
 void a5xx_flush(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct msm_ringbuffer *ring,
 		bool sync)
 {
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
 	struct a5xx_gpu *a5xx_gpu = to_a5xx_gpu(adreno_gpu);
 	uint32_t wptr;
 	unsigned long flags;
 
 	/*
 	 * Most flush operations need to issue a WHERE_AM_I opcode to sync up
 	 * the rptr shadow
 	 */
 	if (sync)
 		update_shadow_rptr(gpu, ring);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ring->preempt_lock, flags);
 
 	/* Copy the shadow to the actual register */
 	ring->cur = ring->next;
 
 	/* Make sure to wrap wptr if we need to */
 	wptr = get_wptr(ring);
 
-	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->preempt_lock, flags);
-
 	/* Make sure everything is posted before making a decision */
 	mb();
 
 	/* Update HW if this is the current ring and we are not in preempt */
 	if (a5xx_gpu->cur_ring == ring && !a5xx_in_preempt(a5xx_gpu))
 		gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_CP_RB_WPTR, wptr);
+
+	/* Do not let a preemption update overwrite this with an older WPTR. */
+	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->preempt_lock, flags);
 }
 
